cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Feret: A Python Module to calculate the Feret Diameter of Binary Images"
abstract: >-
  Python module for exact calculation of the maximum and minimum Feret
  diameters (and the diameters 90° to each) of binary images. Results
  match ImageJ when using pixel-edge mode and are computed exactly rather
  than approximated.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Neuwirth-Trapp"
    given-names: "Matthias"
    email: "mneuwirth@ethz.ch"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-5320-6354"
version: "1.4.0"
date-released: "2026-07-31"
url: "https://github.com/matthiasnwt/feret"
repository-code: "https://github.com/matthiasnwt/feret"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - feret diameter
  - maxferet
  - minferet
  - binary image
  - image analysis
  - caliper diameter
  - python
